    "durationMs": 215167,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `app/Models/Link.php` + migration: `links` table with unique `code`, `url` (text, stored verbatim), atomic `clicks` counter\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php`: create (generated 8-char alnum code when omitted), show, redirect, list\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php`: routes registered at root (`apiPrefix: ''`), so `/links` and `/r/{code}` — no `/api` prefix; validation exceptions render as `{\"error\": \"...\"}` with 422\n- Validation: `url:http,https` (absolute http/https with host — verified against the framework's regex) and code regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`; duplicate custom codes return 409 (existence check plus unique-index race guard)\n- Clicks increment via a single atomic SQL `UPDATE ... clicks + 1` on every `/r/{code}` hit\n\n**Verified end-to-end** (via `sh start.sh` against the real MySQL, then full restart)\n- 201 create / 409 duplicate / 404 unknown (with `error` field) / 302 redirect with exact `Location` header / `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in creation order\n- 422 for missing/invalid url, bad codes (3, 21-char, spaces, invalid chars), and malformed JSON\n- Links and click counts survived a full server restart; new redirects still increment\n\n**Quality gates**: 12 feature tests passing (60 assertions), Pint clean, server logs error-free. Test rows were deleted afterward, so the API starts with an empty table. The README now documents startup (`sh start.sh`) and all endpoints."
  }
